  "elenco": [
   {
    "frase": "1 ▸) is a highly selective BCL-2 inhibitor first approved in the United States, and later in the EU, for monotherapy of chronic lymphocytic leukaemia in patients with 17p deletion or TP53 mutation (Salem et al., 2017 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "1",
     "2",
     "2017"
    ],
    "n": 3
   },
   {
    "frase": "Deeks, 2016 ▸) and later the approval extended to acute myeloid leukaemia and small lymphocytic lymphoma (European Medicines Agency, 2016 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2016",
     "2016"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "The mechanism of action focuses on triggering and restoring apoptosis in tumour cells by releasing pro-apoptotic proteins from the BCL2 family (Konopleva et al., 2006 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2006"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Venetoclax belongs to class IV of the Biopharmaceutical Classification System, indicating low solubility (<4 ng ml−1) and low permeability (Emami Riedmaier et al., 2018 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2018"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Absolute bioavailability estimation is only 5.4% of the administered dose (Alaarg et al., 2022 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2022"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Various methods, including chemical and physical modifications, are employed to enhance solubility (Mantri et al., 2017 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2017"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Chemical modifications involve salt formation, complexation and hydrophilic group introduction (Skořepová et al., 2017 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2017"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Skořepová et al., 2016 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2016"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Koehl et al., 2022 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2022"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Guillory, 2003 ▸), while physical changes include particle size reduction, carrier dispersion and crystal state modification (Mantri et al., 2017 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2003",
     "2017"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "Zvoníček et al., 2018 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2018"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Skořepová et al., 2014 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2014"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Bernstein, 2011 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2011"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Brittain, 2009 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2009"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Polymorphs are distinct crystal structures, exhibiting different molecular arrangements and packing within their crystal lattice while keeping the same chemical composition (Brittain, 2009 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2009"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "The traditional way to explore polymorphism is by crystallization from various solvents, obtaining the possible forms, and investigating their potential for further use (Hilfiker, 2006 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2006"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "These can be classified into different categories based on the variability of the amount of entrapped solvent, such as stoichiometric/non-stoichiometric (Tieger, Kiss, Pokol, Finta, Dušek et al., 2016 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2016"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Tieger, Kiss, Pokol, Finta, Rohlíček et al., 2016 ▸), or structure, for example, channel/cavity (Te, 2001 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2016",
     "2001"
    ],
    "n": 2
   },
   {
    "frase": "Price et al., 2006 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2006"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Sládková et al., 2015 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2015"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Zvoníček et al., 2017 ▸) solvates.",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2017"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "They exhibit distinct and, in some cases, beneficial physical and chemical properties compared with their non-solvated counterparts (Byrn, 2017 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2017"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Moreover, they may be less stable due to potential desolvation during manufacturing (Caira et al., 2007 ▸), which can lead to changes in the drug’s properties.",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2007"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "The desolvation process can produce either nonsolvated forms or hydrates, as water for hydrate formation can be obtained from the natural humidity of the surrounding environment (Bhattacharya & Saha, 2013 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2013"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Minkov et al., 2014 ▸;",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2014"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "Nicolaï et al., 2007 ▸).",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
     "2007"
    ],
    "n": 1
   },
   {
    "frase": "On the other hand, in some cases, the use of solvates as intermediates can be advantageous (Bhattacharya & Saha, 2013 ▸), as certain solvated forms can lower processing temperatures, aiding in techniques like hot-melt ex",
    "numeri_non_coperti": [
